# --- s029 Book I d.5 q.1 = Ord. I d.5 p.1 q.un. (Vat. nn.1-45)
n("n500","s029-01","Circa quintam distinctionem","la","source","= *Ord.* I d. 5 p. 1 q. un. (ed. Vat. IV, nn. 1–45), *utrum essentia divina generet vel generetur*.","certain")
n("n501","s029-01","8. de trini.","la","source","Richard of St Victor, *De Trin.* VI c. 22 (ed. Vat. n. 2), not book VIII. B agrees with A (*viij. de trini.*), so the error is in the common text. Richard's polemic (*in morem Goliae*) is aimed at the Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 5 c. 1.","certain")
n("n502","s029-01","extra de summa tri. et fide catholica","la","source","*X* 1.1.2 (*Damnamus*), Lateran IV (1215), condemning Joachim of Fiore's *libellus* against the Lombard (ed. Vat. nn. 8–12).","certain")
n("n503","s029-02","Et est Adam li. 1. di. 33. q. 4.","la","source","**A reader's key to sources, in Gorris's own voice.** He says that the argument *res generans etc.* (*Ord.* n. 13) ‘is Adam’, i.e. probably Adam Wodeham, I d. 33 q. 4. B agrees (*Et est adam li. i. di. xxxiij. q. iiij.*). The Vatican edition traces the argument to Henry and Godfrey and does not name Adam. The reference is not identified: either Wodeham's Oxford *Lectura* or the abbreviation by Henry Totting of Oyta (Paris 1512), whose numbering may differ. If it is Wodeham, Gorris is reading Scotus alongside a fourteenth-century source.","to-verify")
n("n504","s029-02","hic doctor est Henricus in summa","la","source","Gorris identifies the anonymous *quidam doctor* of *Ord.* n. 35 (*repetit opiniones aliorum, primam…*) as Henry of Ghent, *Summa* (a. 54? cf. a. 58 q. 2 on *essentia est pater Filii*). The Vatican apparatus names Henry, *Summa* a. 54 q. 5 [sic?], as the source of the opinions of Alexander and Praepositinus recited there.","to-verify")
n("n505","s029-03","c. damnamus","la","source","*X* 1.1.2. The account of Joachim's two errors (the charge of *quaternitas* against the Lombard; a merely collective, *similitudinaria* unity) follows *Ord.* nn. 8–11.","certain")
n("n506","s029-03","Volo pater vt sint vnum in nobis sicut et nos vnum sumus","la","source","John 17:21–22, conflated (*ut omnes unum sint… ut sint unum sicut et nos unum sumus*). It is quoted in *Damnamus* and at *Ord.* n. 9.","certain")
n("n507","s029-04","Sed veniendo ad opinionem magistri et Scoti et finaliter fidelium","la","commentary","Gorris names Scotus in the third person here (*magistri et Scoti*), while elsewhere *doctor* is Scotus. This marks the text as Gorris's compilation and not a mere abbreviation.","certain")
n("n508","s029-04","in epistola ad Volusianum","la","source","**Misattribution, shared by B** (*in epistola ad volusianum*). *Evangelio non crederem nisi me catholicae Ecclesiae commoveret auctoritas* is Aug. *Contra epistolam Fundamenti* c. 5 n. 6, correctly cited by Scotus at *Ord.* n. 26. Gorris has substituted the letter to Volusianus (*Ep.* 137).","certain")
n("n509","s029-05","quandocunque est aliquod subiectum vltimate abstractum","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 5 n. 18 (*quandocumque subiectum est abstractum ultimata abstractione, de eo nihil praedicatur nisi quod est de ratione eius*), with nn. 19–24.","certain")
n("n510","s029-05","Actiones sunt suppositorum","la","source","*Actiones sunt suppositorum*: proverbial, from Arist. *Metaph.* I 1 (981a16–17, *actiones… omnes circa singulare sunt*), as in the *Auctoritates Aristotelis*.","certain")
n("n511","s029-06","nec conseruans","la","textual","*conseruans* is unexpected after *generans*, but B has it too (*nec generans nec conseruans*). Perhaps a slip in the common archetype for *generata* or *spirans*, or a deliberate extension to an *actio ad extra*.","uncertain")
n("n512","s029-07","nec est materia nec quasi materia","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 5 p. 2 nn. 93–97 (*tenendo cum doctoribus antiquis… nullus ausus fuit ponere materiam*), anticipated here from the next question.","certain")
n("n513","s029-08","in substantia est tantum vna abstractio","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 5 nn. 19–22: one abstraction in substances, two in absolute accidents, three in relations; the *ultima abstractio* is of the quiddity.","certain")
n("n514","s029-08","homo et risibile non quoad omnia conuertuntur","la","source","Cf. *Ord.* I d. 5 nn. 23 and 34 (subject and attribute). The point that aptitude is predicated of *risibile* but not of *homo* is Gorris's gloss.","certain")
n("n515","s029-08","Ad Ricardum dicitur quod eius auctoritas hic non tenetur","la","source","*Ord.* n. 26: *nego Richardum tenendo Magistrum*, on the authority of the Church (*Damnamus*).","certain")
n("n532","s029-03","ergo secundum opinionem Joachim essencia generat et generatur","la","variant","B omits the sentence (*…nec generat nec generatur. Secundus error…*). Also in this paragraph: A *indiuisibilis*, B *indiuiduabilis*.","certain")

# --- B collation (full): B41R–B43L
upd("n509", append=" B reads *Quantumcunque*, an error for A's *quandocunque*.")
